    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65082,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Yolk sac tumour, prepubertal type; mature teratoma NOS; dermoid cyst NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65083,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vagina, paravaginal space</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65084,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vaginal yolk sac tumour (YST) usually occurs in children aged &lt;&nbsp;4&nbsp;years {6086471; 30814243; 22178761}. Most patients present with vaginal bleeding and have a polypoid mass on examination {22178761; 23361494}. Serum AFP is elevated. Vaginal mature teratoma has been reported in patients aged 15&ndash;30&nbsp;years and presents with a vaginal or paravaginal mass lesion {12704753; 25671703; 1892423}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65085,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Primary vaginal germ cell tumours are very rare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65086,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65087,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Germ cell tumours of the vagina probably arise from pluripotent germ cells in the extragonadal midline as a result of stalled or aberrant migration {27631522}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65088,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vaginal YSTs measure 1.4&ndash;6&nbsp;cm and have a soft, greyish-tan cut surface, often with necrosis and haemorrhage {6086471; 30814243; 22178761}. Mature teratomas typically have a cystic cut surface {12704753; 25671703; 1892423}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65089,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The histopathology of germ cell tumours of the vagina is identical to that of their ovarian counterparts.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65090,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65091,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65092,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> characteristic microscopic and immunohistochemical features, as seen in their ovarian counterparts.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65093,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vaginal YSTs are staged the same way as other vaginal primaries.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65094,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 360,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vaginal YSTs are malignant, but most patients achieve complete remission with combination chemotherapy (with or without surgical resection) {22178761; 30814243; 16200632}. Vaginal mature teratomas are benign.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:15:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]